{
  "description": "Per-bin CLI contract fixture for #3342's opt-in JSON error envelope. Discovered bins (every bin/idd-*.mjs) are cross-checked against this table's `bins` keys by tests/helper-cli-contract.test.mts -- a bin missing here fails the test, and deleting any single row does too. #3346 completed the migration onto runHelperCli for every packaged bin; structural migration coverage now lives in the repository inventory audit. runs.unknownFlag / runs.noArgs record the documented exitCode/kind for the two standard contract runs (an unknown flag, and no arguments at all) against a fake gh that always fails; the unknownFlag run must be kind usage. extraScenarios lists additional named, bin-specific runs beyond the two standard ones, each with valid arguments that let the helper reach a (fake, always-failing) gh call: pre-merge-readiness's ghTransportFailure503 (the #2806 case, asserting its existing {\"error\": ...} stdout JSON and exit code 1 stay unchanged while its envelope kind is now transport), and discover-readiness-check / discover-viability-gate / authoring-owner-provenance / resume-claim-routing's ghTransportFailure503ViaProviderPort (a regression case, #3342: none of these four call gh-exec.mts directly for their issue lookup -- they go through ProviderPort.getWorkItem(), whose non-404 failure path wraps the original gh-exec.mts-tagged error as `.cause` on a brand-new Error, so classifyHelperError must walk the cause chain to classify it as transport instead of losing it to internal -- observed against the built bins before that walk existed: the same args against a fake `gh: HTTP 503` reported `kind: internal`). resume-claim-routing's own row additionally sets `ghScript` (see tests/helper-cli-contract.test.mts's ExtraScenario.ghScript doc comment): its runCli calls resolveViewerLogin and listWorkItemComments before getWorkItem -- both ProviderPort methods that pass gh-exec.mts's tagged error straight through unwrapped, unlike getWorkItem's own toProviderError re-wrap -- so the shared always-fails stub would fail on one of those first and never actually exercise the .cause-wrapped path this scenario exists to cover; this row's own gh script lets both succeed and fails only the issue lookup.",
